language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session1_magic_square: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A magic square is an n x n grid (n is not 2) in which each cell holds a different integer from 1 to n^2 and
$ the sum of the integers in each row, column and diagonal is the same, namely n(n^2+1)/2. Find a magic square for the
$ given size n.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `session1_magic_square.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session1_magic_square.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `session1_magic_square_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py session1_magic_square.json
$   savilerow model.eprime session1_magic_square_1.param -run-solver

$ n: the side length of the square
given n : int(1..)

$ the common sum of each row, column and diagonal
letting magic_sum = n*(n*n+1)/2

$ square[i,j]: the number in row i and column j (indices from 1)
find square : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n*n)

such that
$ each cell holds a different integer, so together they are 1 to n^2
allDiff(flatten(square)),
$ every row sums to n(n^2+1)/2
forAll i : int(1..n) . (sum j : int(1..n) . square[i,j]) = magic_sum,
$ every column sums to n(n^2+1)/2
forAll j : int(1..n) . (sum i : int(1..n) . square[i,j]) = magic_sum,
$ the main diagonal sums to n(n^2+1)/2
(sum i : int(1..n) . square[i,i]) = magic_sum,
$ the other diagonal sums to n(n^2+1)/2
(sum i : int(1..n) . square[i,n+1-i]) = magic_sum
